* {{audio|en|En-ca-hemlock.oga|a=Canada}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# Any of the [[poisonous]] [[umbellifer]]ous [[plant]]s, of the genera
## {{taxfmt|Conium|genus}}, either {{taxfmt|Conium maculatum|species}} or {{taxlink|Conium chaerophylloides|species}}.
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1940|author=Rosetta E. Clarkson|title=Green Enchantments: The Magic Spell of Gardens |publisher=The Macmillan Company|page=273|text=Have a tree or two the witches particularly like, such as the alder, larch, cypress and '''hemlock'''; then, to counteract any possible evil effects, there must be a holly, yew, hazel, elder, mountain ash or juniper.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1971|author=[[w:Richard Carpenter (screenwriter)|Richard Carpenter]]|title=Catweazle and the Magic Zodiac|publisher=Puffin Books|location=Harmondsworth|page=41|text=There were bunches of wild garlic to keep out evil spirits, foxgloves for healing spells and '''hemlock''' and vervain for darker magic.}}
## {{taxfmt|Cicuta|genus}}, [[water hemlock]] plant.
# The [[poison]] obtained from these {{taxfmt|Conium|genus}} and {{taxfmt|Cicuta|genus}} plants. {{defdate|from c. 1600}}
# {{senseid|en|Tsuga}} Any of several [[coniferous]] [[tree]]s, of the genus {{taxfmt|Tsuga|genus}}, that grow in [[North America]]; the [[wood]] of such trees. {{defdate|from 1670}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018|author=w:Richard Powers| title=w:The Overstory| publisher=Vintage (2019)| page=380| passage=The wind blows and the '''hemlocks''' wave their feathery leading shoots. Such a graceful profile, so elegant a tree.}}

